  "result": {
    "brief": "## Verdict\n\nThe handoff is accurate enough to execute from on structure and diagnosis, but **not** on its numbers or its Phase 0 commands: the node census is exact, the unit census is wrong in five places, the edge total is a double-counted row count, and all three Phase 0 steps are unsafe or built on a false premise as written. The single most important correction is that **Phase 0 must not be run verbatim** — step 1's `.gitignore` rule does not match `.backups/` (`.gitignore:7` is `backups/`, no dot), leaving the 82 MB root backup store stageable, and step 2's stated remote state is wrong (`git ls-remote --heads origin` returns five heads, not one). Before any of that, do the one genuinely urgent thing the handoff buries in Phase 2: add `index` to `SKIP_DIRS`, because 518 of the 522 latest `index/` manifest records carry a falsy `phase` and will be re-embedded into the live corpus on the next routine ingest.\n\n## Corrections to the handoff\n\n| Handoff claim | Actual | Evidence (path:line) |\n|---|---|---|\n| HANDOFF:87 \"Healthy — 11\" | 13 rows in the table; 14 with Aristotle. 13+5+4+4+1 = 27 only if the header reads 13 | plans/index-system-HANDOFF-2026-07-28.md:87 vs body :91-103 |\n| HANDOFF:23 \"357 unit records\" | Reconciles with nothing. §4's own units column sums to 323; corrected per-entry derivation = 310 | HANDOFF:23 vs :91-103 (252) + :105 (45) + :111-115 (0) + :123-126 (26) |\n| HANDOFF:96 BT 18 units | 17 — the 18th `.json` is `manifest.json` | corpus/index/Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-structured/manifest.json (`total_units: 17`, `len(units)=17`) |\n| HANDOFF:97 BCAP 14 units | 13 | .../Heidegger - Basic Concepts of Aristotelian Philosophy/bcap-structured/manifest.json (`total_units: 13`) |\n| HANDOFF:100 Uexküll 15 units | 14 — verified this session: `python3 -c` on manifest → `14 14` | corpus/index/Von Uexkull - A Foray.../uex-structured/manifest.json |\n| HANDOFF:103 Wendt 7 units | 8 (`dfd-00`..`dfd-07`) — an *under*count, opposite direction to the four above | .../Wendt - Design for Dasein/_synthesis/manifest.json |\n| HANDOFF:105 Aristotle 45 units | 34 structured records; the extra 11 are 9 `*-greek.json` + greek-appendix + bekker-index | corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/manifest.json (34-element list) |\n| HANDOFF:23, :242 \"17,736 edge-CSV rows\" | A row count that double-counts nearly every edge (`_synthesis/global-edges.csv` re-serializes the per-source files). ~9,762 distinct triples; and 19,770 rows actually on disk — the `*-edges.csv` glob misses 2,034 (RM ships 8 files named plain `edges.csv`; GM and In-Game ship `global-edges-pre-canonical.csv`) | Wendt control: units/*-edges.csv 307 rows/305 distinct = _synthesis/global-edges.csv 307/305, intersection 305 |\n| HANDOFF:138 \"seven silent-skip sites\" | 17 in-branch content-discarding sites (22 counting structural omissions and trivial guards). The 1A estimate and Gate C1 are sized against the wrong number | scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:260, :346, :430, :546, :559, :596, :650, :690, :727, :827, :837, :1110, :1120, :1128, :1267, :1290, :1300 |\n| HANDOFF:142 \"`parse_ontology_md` returns `[]`\" | No such function exists. Real entry points: `parse_table_ontology` (:195), `parse_header_ontology` (:513), `_parse_field_value_ontology` (:292). The substance holds for all three | `grep -rn parse_ontology_md` → no match |\n| HANDOFF:161 doc_id at `run_ingest_phase2.py:220-222` | :221-223 (:220 is blank). `:659`/`:699` are exact | scripts/ingest/run_ingest_phase2.py:221-223 |\n| HANDOFF:171 \"One collection, `knowledge_chunks`… filtered by `where`\" | Five Chroma collections exist (`local_vectors_1536`, `god_agent_vectors_1536`, `knowledge_chunks`, `v2_knowledge_chunks`, `dissertation-perplexity-cache`). Only `knowledge_chunks` is ever queried — but **no** production code emits a `where` on the `collection` field; every live filter is `author_raw` or `title_raw` | vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3 `select id,name from collections`; retrieval-stage.ts:208,:261,:286,:340; icp-orchestrator.ts:390 |\n| HANDOFF:174 \"Boredom Secondary (68)\" | 68 is a label-*attribution* count (§9 recipe, 771 attributions); only 61 node objects carry it as their sole `text`. Same denominator slip as D6's \"199 of 701\" | corpus/index/compiled-index.json grouped by `text`: 61; §9 recipe: 68 |\n| HANDOFF:157 \"`deriveAuthor` splits the display label… renaming breaks author-scoped retrieval\" | Entry directory names never reach `deriveAuthor` — it receives hook `sourceText`/`targetText`, which come from `ARISTOTLE_WORK_MAP` (:136-147) and `_infer_target_text()` (:1050-1070). The real coupling is `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1239` `aristotle_dir = CORPUS_INDEX / \"Aristotle - Complete Works\"` — rename that one directory and all 72 hooks vanish | cross-author-utils.ts:395-398; compile-corpus-index.py:1239, :1246 |\n| HANDOFF:197 \"`git ls-remote --heads origin` lists only `writing-pipeline-v2`\" | Five heads: audit-fixes, god-agent-v2, god-agent-v2-pr, main, writing-pipeline-v2. Origin carries **zero** tags against 83 local. Also: `pre-promotion-20260419`'s target commit is already reachable from origin/writing-pipeline-v2, so that push carries no new history | `git ls-remote --heads origin` (run this session, 5 refs); `git ls-remote --tags origin` → empty, exit 0 |\n| HANDOFF:196 verify with `git status --short corpus/index \\| wc -l` | Returns **27** — git collapses untracked directories. The metric cannot distinguish success from doing nothing. Use `--untracked-files=all` (1512 now) | `git status --short corpus/index \\| wc -l` → 27 |\n| HANDOFF:218 \"458 hits, of which 39 are embedded prompt text\" | Different units: 458 = `strings` *lines*; 39 = metadata *rows*. Raw byte occurrences 497; live-table occurrences 319. The 39 live in `god_agent_vectors_1536`, not `knowledge_chunks`, so rebuilding the corpus collection never clears them | `strings -a vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3 \\| grep -c corpus/index` → 458; `grep -a -o` → 497 |\n| HANDOFF:230 ig-10 \"one unclosed object, lines 107–155\" | Bracket-*type* mismatch at :155 only. Verified: :134 opens `\"non_game_studies_anchor_theories\": {`, :155 closes with `],`. `expected_game_loci` (:107-119) is well-formed and not implicated. **One-character fix** | `sed -n '134p;155p'` on corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-incorporation.json |\n| HANDOFF:236 \"install `mmdc` (render validation has **never** run)\" | mmdc 11.14.0 is installed at `/home/dalton/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/bin/mmdc`, and validation *has* run twice. The real gap: 13 of 15 `.mmd`-bearing entries lack a record | `which mmdc`; corpus/index/Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary (1985-2017)/_synthesis/render-validation.txt; corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/render-validation.txt |\n| HANDOFF:208 \"three shape adapters\" | Five `cluster-ontology.json` files in four/five shapes. Boredom Secondary ships a compiler-native one (`nodeCount: 68`, `generatedBy: parse_header_ontology`) and VR Pedagogy a minimal `{cluster, nodes[60]}`. Both entries already register via markdown → wiring their JSON double-counts 128 nodes | `find corpus/index -name cluster-ontology.json` → 5 |\n| HANDOFF:246 Gate W1 \"his 15 units\" | 14, per the entry's own manifest; the plan says 14. A gate whose pass condition is a disputed integer gets argued, not measured | uex-structured/manifest.json → `14 14` |\n| HANDOFF:65 \"No source file has been modified. No code written.\" | True for corpus/index (zero byte drift since capture). False for the programme's own tooling: `wc -l < scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` = **1412**, `git show HEAD:… \\| wc -l` = **1397** (+3 TEXT_DIRS entries uncommitted). Also `run_ingest_phase2.py` +206/-69, `verify_ingest.py` +18/-4, `manifest.jsonl` +882, `.gitignore` +1 | commands above; `git status --short` |\n\n## New findings the handoff missed\n\nRanked by severity.\n\n**1 — BLOCKER (Phase 0, today). The next routine ingest floods the live corpus with ~2,100 index chunks.** `SKIP_DIRS` contains no `index` entry in any of the three walkers (`scripts/ingest/run_ingest_phase2.py:978`, `run_ingest.py:365`, `parallel_ingest.py:69` — all verbatim `{\".extracted_media\", \"__pycache__\", \"node_modules\", \".git\", \".ingest_cache\"}`), and `should_skip_phase2` (:312-331) requires `int(rec.get(\"phase\") or 0) >= 2`. Measured this session: of 522 distinct latest `index/` manifest records, **518 have a falsy `phase`** → all re-ingested. The index's own analytical prose then competes with source material in every retrieval. This is Phase 2's R2.6, a three-line change, sitting behind the highest-blast-radius phase in the programme.\n\n**2 — BLOCKER (Phase 0). The handoff's own evidence base rests on a dirty tree.** Every §5 `path:line` citation and the entire §4 census resolve against the working tree, not HEAD: compiler 1412 vs 1397 lines, 19 vs 16 registered entries; `corpus/index/compiled-index.json` is tracked and dirty (+583/-55; worktree 701 nodes/1722 terms, HEAD 670/1663). A `git checkout` or `git stash` on those two paths silently invalidates the handoff wholesale.\n\n**3 — BLOCKER (Phase 1). The compiler emits zero `warn()` calls on the current corpus while discarding 55 tension records.** Its docstring (:14-15) promises warnings to stderr; a monkey-patched run counted 0. It also has **no exit-code discipline at all** — no `sys.exit`, no counter, no `--strict`; `main()` at :1361 always returns 0. A clean-looking run is not evidence of a clean compile.\n\n**4 — BLOCKER (Phase 1). Gate C1 \"two consecutive runs byte-identical\" is unachievable regardless of the sort fix.** `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:1375` writes `\"builtAt\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()` unconditionally. 1A/C1.7 is scoped to `canonicalTerms` only. Enforce the gate literally and Phase 1 never exits.\n\n**5 — BLOCKER (Phase 1). The unreachable `break` at :718-721 is a general parser bug, not a Rickert one-off.** Verified: `elif current_key and stripped:` (:718) precedes `elif stripped.startswith(\"###\") or …: break` (:720-721), so once any field key is seen the break can never fire. The last field of the last node in *any* header section absorbs the rest of the file — today one `centralityTier` holds 10,009 chars of a dumped edge table and its `units` array holds 973 garbage tokens. **C1.8 \"strip parse pollution\" treats the symptom**; reordering two `elif` arms is the fix.\n\n**6 — BLOCKER (Phase 1 exposure, fix scheduled Phase 5). `_hooksDerivationDone` starts failing the moment Phase 1 begins recompiling.** `cross-author-utils.ts:56` one-shot flag, guard :342, set :351 — grep across `src/` and `tests/` returns only those three lines; no reset exists. `jsonl-loaders.ts:205-213` invalidates on mtime and returns a *fresh* graph; 0 of 72 hooks carry a `sourceAuthor` key, so derivation at :344-349 is the only source. Recompile mid-process → empty `requiredAuthors` → `icp-orchestrator.ts:368` `continue` → cross-author backfill silently disabled, no log line. A second uninvalidated cache compounds it: `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:794` `if (this.protectedTerms) return this.protectedTerms`, with its own bypass read at :798.\n\n**7 — BLOCKER (Phase 2). `R2.5` \"purge before move\" has no implementation, and the built-in cleanup no-ops on exactly this operation.** The only delete in the ingest tree is `run_ingest_phase2.py:1830 coll.delete(ids=_stale)`, fed by `coll.get(where={\"path_rel\": path_rel})` at :1686 — which returns zero rows once the path changes. `ls scripts/ingest/` contains no purge script, and no phase backs up the 6.5 GB `vector_db_1536/` before a first-run destructive operation.\n\n**8 — BLOCKER (Phase 2). Gate R1's two clauses contradict each other, and its second clause is unpassable.** R2.4 rewrites 772 manifest `path_rel` values *to* the new path; Gate R1 requires zero records *under* the new path. Separately, 296 files inside corpus/index contain the literal string `corpus/index` in their own prose (1,800 line-hits), 219 of them already ingested `ok` — so any re-ingestion reproduces them all.\n\n**9 — HIGH (Phase 2/5). Manifest and vector store have already diverged for `index/`.** The manifest marks 522 index documents `ok` with 2,134 chunks, but zero of their `doc_id`s exist in `vector_db_1536`; the only index chunks present are 25 from 6 PDFs under `Game-Behavior Analysis Method`. \"Manifest clean\" and \"store clean\" are independent facts and Gate R1 tests only the first.\n\n**10 — HIGH (Phase 0/6). `corpus/` itself (2.7 GB, 288 source PDFs) has no backup and no tracking.** `git ls-files corpus | grep -v '^corpus/index/'` → 0; 3,079 untracked non-index paths, none gitignored. That is the entire input to Phase 6.\n\n**11 — HIGH (Phase 5). `npm run build` cannot succeed — `npx tsc --noEmit` reports 157 errors.** So the `FacetedRetrieval` TS2554 arity bug (`faceted-retrieval.ts:158,190`) can never surface in CI. Everything runs through `tsx` (transpile-only), which is why 4-arg calls to a 3-param method execute silently. And fixing the arity does **not** buy reranking: `hybridSearch` (:324-376) has no rerank path at all and hardcodes `semanticSearch(query, {maxChunks:20, minRelevance:0.6})` at :353-356. Re-scope the item.\n\n**12 — HIGH (Phase 5). `RetrievalOptions.collections` strands 167 real chunks.** `retrieval-stage.ts:189-197` pushes `'textual_analysis'` and `'v2_knowledge_chunks'` into a field that `smart-retrieval-layer.ts` normalizes at :194 and never reads (`opts.collections` appears zero times); `v2_knowledge_chunks` holds 167 chunks unreachable at runtime. Worse, the field means Chroma *collections* at some call sites and metadata *values* at others (`corpus-constraint-builder.ts:251-252`) — wiring it naively makes one field mean two things.\n\n**13 — HIGH (Phase 1). C1.6 \"self-check against manifest-declared counts\" has almost no data to check against.** Of 27 entries, only 5 declare any count field; only 3 declare `total_units`; **zero** declare an expected node count. The single `nodeCount` on disk (Boredom Secondary, 68) was generated by the compiler's own `parse_header_ontology()` — checking the compiler against its own prior output is a tautology.\n\n**14 — MEDIUM (Phase 3/5). Three whole apparatus classes have no adapter and no mention.** 67 `.mmd` files across 15 entries encode 1,544 arrow-edges — and `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` §2 records for both the aristotle-manifest and heidegger-sz families that \"Edges live only in .mmd (open item)\". 144 `cross_pipeline_bridges` entries live in 22 unit JSONs (runtime has 72 hooks, 100% Aristotle, because the compiler globs `*-cross-pipeline-hooks.md` under the Aristotle dir only, :1239-1244). And 35 `*-deep.json` files carry positions/tensions/interlocutors/ratio-catalogs that N3.1's canonical record has no slot for.\n\n**15 — MEDIUM (Phase 0/2). GitHub Actions workflows nobody mentioned will fire.** `.github/workflows/god-audit.yml:5-21` triggers on `corpus/**`, `scripts/ingest/**`, `vector_db_1536/**` and runs `missing_link_detector.py` — one of the four path-join sites R2.3 must change. `.github/workflows/god-learn-qa.yml:41-53` runs `immutability_checker.py --verify`, whose protected list includes `scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` and `god-reason/reasoning.jsonl` — the two files R2.4 and Phase 3 mutate. Zero occurrences of \"github\"/\"workflow\"/\"CI\" in any of the three programme documents.\n\n**16 — MEDIUM (Phase 2). `/god-learn-verify` — Gate R1's own check — mutates the artifact.** `god_learn.py:711-718 cmd_verify` calls `deduplicate_manifest()` first, rewriting `manifest.jsonl` in place (1,182 → ~696 records) and destroying the 248 `status=failed` index rows. It keys on `path_abs`, so post-move old and new paths survive as two keys.\n\n**17 — MEDIUM (Phase 3). `deduplicate_ontology_nodes` merges across different texts by lowercased name.** `compile-corpus-index.py:1319-1321` keys on `node[\"name\"].lower()` with no text component; :1331-1332 concatenates provenance into one string (`Destruktion` → `\"Heidegger - Being and Time; Heidegger and Rhetoric\"`). 771 raw → 701, i.e. 70 nodes absorbed with no per-merge log.\n\n**18 — LOW (Phase 0). 89 files / 6.4 MB live in four *nested* per-entry `.backups/` dirs** (Boredom Secondary, VR Pedagogy, Social Presence, Veri(dis)similitude) — D2's rule would untrack them while the 13 MB tar still carries them. And 8 empty directories exist under corpus/index, which git cannot represent, so D2 does not preserve the tree shape D1 captured.\n\n## Phase 0 — exact readiness\n\n**Do this before all three items** (pulled out of Phase 2 R2.6; ~2 minutes, fully reversible):\n\n```bash\n# add \"index\" to SKIP_DIRS in all three walkers\nscripts/ingest/run_ingest_phase2.py:978\nscripts/ingest/run_ingest.py:365\nscripts/ingest/parallel_ingest.py:69\n```\nRationale: 518/522 latest index manifest records have a falsy `phase` and fail `should_skip_phase2` (:312-331). Risk: none — three dict literals; revert restores prior behaviour exactly; nothing is written, moved, or deleted. Also fix the three walkers' default roots while you are there (`audit_ingest.py:97` and `verify_ingest.py:166` hardcode the absolute `/home/dalton/projects/claudeflow-testing/corpus`; `watch_corpus.py:175` defaults to bare relative `corpus`).\n\n---\n\n### Item 1 — apply tracking policy (D2)\n\n**Safe right now? No. Three defects; all fixable in minutes.**\n\nCurrent facts. `.gitignore:7` is `backups/`, which does not match `.backups/` — `git check-ignore -v --no-index '.backups/x'` exits 1, and `git status --short` shows `?? .backups/` at 82 MB (`du -sh .backups` → 82M, confirmed this session), containing the full 41 MB index mirror *and* the 13 MB tarball. `git ls-files corpus/index` → 335 tracked; `git status --porcelain -uall corpus/index` → 1,511 untracked + 1 modified, 34,999,976 bytes (78 files / 5.7 MB of that is nested `.backups`). Largest untracked file is 450 KB; zero exceed 1 MB, no `.gitattributes`, no LFS — plain git is fine. Exactly one existing rule collides (`.gitignore:34 docs/` matches a path inside VR Pedagogy's `.backups`, which D2 excludes anyway).\n\n**Precise edit.** Replace the handoff's two corpus-scoped rules with one global rule:\n\n```\n.backups/\n```\n\nThis covers root, `plans/`, `scripts/`, `tmp/Dissertation/`, and all four nested per-entry stores, making `corpus/index/**/.backups/` and `corpus/index/.backups/` redundant. Verified by `git -c core.excludesFile=<scratch>` (repo untouched): all 4 nested `.backups` paths ignored, real entry files not ignored, untracked count 1511 → 1433.\n\n**Precise staging command** — explicit pathspec, never `git add -A`:\n\n```bash\ngit add --dry-run corpus/index   # expect 1512 paths before the .backups rule, 1434 after\ngit add corpus/index\n```\n\n**Verification** (replaces HANDOFF:196, which returns 27):\n\n```bash\ngit status --short --untracked-files=all corpus/index | wc -l   # 1512 now → 1 after (or 0 if you also stage compiled-index.json)\ngit ls-files corpus/index | wc -l                               # 335 now → 1768 expected\n```\n\n**What could go wrong.** (a) `git add -A` at repo root stages 11,524 paths including the 82 MB `.backups/` and the 551 MB `tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox/` — `tmp/` appears nowhere in `.gitignore`. (b) `node_modules` is *tracked* (12,695 files in the index despite `.gitignore:36`; 376 currently modified, 5 deleted), so `git commit -a` sweeps a zod version bump into the index-tracking commit — 93% of the modified-file noise is node_modules. (c) `.gitignore` already carries one uncommitted line 38 (`corpus/Virtual Learning Environments/VLE_Survey_Data/`) that will ride along.\n\n**User decision required:** `compiled-index.json` is tracked and dirty (+583/-55) while §5.2 documents it as non-byte-reproducible. Either characterise the diff or exclude the file from this commit and let Phase 1's deterministic-sort work land it. Also state explicitly which paths the Phase 0 commit includes — the handoff's citations depend on the uncommitted `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` (+15 lines), so commit that too or the evidence base is one `git checkout` from invalid.\n\n### Item 2 — push `writing-pipeline-v3` + tag `pre-promotion-20260419`\n\n**Safe right now? The commands are safe; the premise is wrong and the target is arguably the wrong branch. Rewrite before executing.**\n\nCurrent facts (all live, this session). Origin has five heads (`audit-fixes e7bea3a47`, `god-agent-v2 e889b6ecb`, `god-agent-v2-pr 353a0450c`, `main 40b322ff0`, `writing-pipeline-v2 be9272360`) and **zero tags** against 83 local tags. `writing-pipeline-v3` = `1268adbcf` (2026-04-21), no upstream, 3 unique commits, and **11 commits behind** origin/writing-pipeline-v2. The tag's target commit `54c2ba1fe` is already reachable from origin/writing-pipeline-v2, so pushing the tag carries no new history. Meanwhile `feat/wraith-retrieval` — the branch this programme executes on — has no upstream and **11 local-only commits** (`git rev-list --count feat/wraith-retrieval --not --remotes=origin` → 11); repo-wide, 32 commits exist nowhere but this disk. Local `writing-pipeline-v2` has diverged 9 ahead of origin's; `god-agent-v2-pr` is 191 ahead. Seven local branches are absent from origin. Three stashes exist, all rooted on `god-agent-v2-pr`. A second remote `upstream` (`https://github.com/ste-bah/claudeflow-testing.git`) exists and is unmentioned. `.git/FETCH_HEAD` is dated 2026-07-15 — 13 days stale.\n\n```bash\ngit push -u origin feat/wraith-retrieval        # the 11 commits that actually matter\ngit push origin writing-pipeline-v3             # 3 commits, stale side branch\ngit push origin pre-promotion-20260419          # tag object only, no new history\n```\n\n**What could go wrong.** `writing-pipeline-v3` is checked out as a worktree at `tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox/src-worktree` with 12 uncommitted changes — pushing sends the committed tip, not what that directory contains.\n\n**User decision required:** memory rule `feedback-archon-push-from-wsl-only` + HANDOFF:199 standing rule — ask before each push. We are on WSL, so the machine constraint is satisfied. Confirm which of the three pushes to make.\n\n### Item 3 — back up `production-sandbox/data/` off-machine\n\n**Safe right now? The backup is safe; the gate as worded cannot be met, and the expensive half has no backup at all.**\n\nCurrent facts. `tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox/data/` = 50 MB, 105 files + 2 symlinks, untracked and not gitignored (`git ls-files` → 0). `data/corpus` = 49 MB, 4,939 claims across 24 `claims.jsonl` files — **no backup anywhere on this machine**; the 79 snapshots under `production-sandbox/.backups/` cover `data/gold` only and all sit on `/dev/sdd` alongside the original. Gold set is 25/20 (`resolver-gold-dev.jsonl` 25 lines, `resolver-gold-holdout.jsonl` 20), matching HANDOFF:260. `/mnt/nas` and `/mnt/j` exist as directories but are **not mounted** — both `df -h` to `/dev/sdd`, the root volume. Real mounts: `/mnt/f` (8.6T), `/mnt/m` (9.1T), `/mnt/h`, `/mnt/i`, `/mnt/c`, `/mnt/d`. Disk headroom: 233 G free of 1007 G.\n\n**Precise command** — back up the *whole* tree; measured, it gzips to 7,928,893 bytes:\n\n```bash\ncd tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox\ntar -czf /tmp/sandbox-data-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ).tar.gz data   # no -h\ncd /tmp && sha256sum sandbox-data-*.tar.gz > sandbox-data-*.tar.gz.sha256   # RELATIVE path\nscp both files to dalton@192.168.50.243 (CHIMERA) or daltonsalvo@192.168.50.10 (Mac)\nssh <host> 'sha256sum -c sandbox-data-*.tar.gz.sha256'                      # verify AT DESTINATION\n```\n\n**What could go wrong.** (a) Size-optimising is actively unsafe: `data/corpus` holds two *relative* symlinks (`compiled-index.json -> compiled-index.v2.json`, `ontology-embeddings.jsonl -> ontology-embeddings.v1.jsonl`); excluding the large derived artifacts drops the archive to 1.8 MB and leaves both dangling. Do not use `tar -h` either — it doubles the archive. (b) Do not repeat the absolute-path mistake in `.backups/corpus-index-full-20260728T230859Z.tar.gz.sha256`, which only verifies at that exact path. (c) Verifying at the source proves nothing.\n\n**User decision required:** what \"second location\" means. If a real second machine is unavailable, `/mnt/m` (9.1T, real 9p mount) is the least-bad fallback and should be recorded as a **partial** Gate P0 pass, not a pass.\n\n**What is genuinely solid.** §2's backup claims all hold, and better than claimed: manifests identical (1,848 = 1,848), the §2 re-verification recipe returns `INTACT` exit 0, `sha256sum -c` on the tarball returns OK (`878a8192…1ea3fe`), and the live tree has **not drifted a single byte** since capture — 1,848 files / 41,711,698 bytes still hash-for-hash identical to `MANIFEST-source`. D1 is done. Restoring is safe.\n\n## Ordering call\n\n**Keep P1 before P2. Change P2's position: move it to after P5, and split R2.6/R2.7 forward into Phase 0.**\n\nP2's stated justification — \"sequenced before normalization and wiring so those target final paths\" (HANDOFF:216) — does not survive inspection. P5's coupling to the location is *one constant plus one line*: `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:31` `CORPUS_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\"` (+ `:32` output) and `src/god-agent/shared/jsonl-loaders.ts:200` `resolve(root, 'corpus', 'index', 'compiled-index.json')`. P4 is content editing addressed relative to entry directories — the tree's parent is irrelevant. P3's only path coupling is N3.5, which extends `scripts/normalize-edges.py` past the five hardcoded literals at `:37-41` — the *same five lines* R2.9 hand-edits, so running P2 first means editing five strings that N3.5 then deletes.\n\nAgainst that thin benefit, P2 at position 2 costs a great deal:\n\n- **It invalidates the programme's own evidence base mid-flight.** R2.10 sweeps 297 index files + 47 live plans + 389 tmp files, including `plans/index-system-report-2026-07-28.md` (11 hits) — the document HANDOFF:11 names as the evidence base P3 and P4 execute against.\n- **It buries P4's content diffs.** The sweep rewrites 297 files inside corpus/index at exactly the point P4 starts editing entry content; nothing distinguishes mechanical path churn from real repair.\n- **Its gate is self-contradictory and its purge does not exist** (findings 7, 8).\n- **It requires a full re-ingest to prove Gate R1** while `:8000`, `:8001`, `:8002` are all down — confirmed this session, `curl` returns HTTP `000` on all three, and `.run/*.pid` (5972/6008/6555) are stale with no `/proc` entries. No phase lists `/god-launch` as a prerequisite.\n\nThe one durable argument *for* the move is Phase 6's §6C rationale — with every source a standalone entry, an index living inside `corpus/` would need entries for itself. That is a real reason, and it is never given as P2's reason. If the move is kept, adopt that justification and schedule it where it belongs: after P5, as a single mechanical commit on a settled tree.\n\nTwo further sequencing changes I would make:\n\n1. **Promote 4A ahead of P3.** Gate N1 requires \"all 494 JSON files parse\", but the single failing file is repaired in P4. 4A is small: ig-10 is one character (`],` → `},` at :155), plus the VLE path at `vle-05-…md:3`, plus parsers for the four divergent tension schemas (`pole_A`/`pole_B`; `wendt_position`/`against`; two label/description-only forms — none carry the `node_a`/`node_b` pair the guard at :1128-1129 requires, which is how 55 of 119 records vanish).\n2. **Move the three runtime-state fixes out of W5.7 into Phase 1.** `_hooksDerivationDone` starts failing on the first recompile (finding 6). Leaving it at P5 means four phases of drafting sessions silently losing a retrieval path, precisely while the index is supposedly being improved.\n\nOptional but high-value: a **Phase 1.5 thin wiring spike** — an additive, default-off entry-scope read path over the six entries that already have structured units on disk (Uexküll 14, BT 17, BCAP 13, FCM 15, Rickert 10, Wendt 8 = 77 unit JSONs), needing no relocation, no normalization, no repair. It answers the question the whole programme bets on — does unit-level content in the drafting prompt change output quality? — in days rather than after 26–38 claimed prerequisite days, and produces the volume evidence W5.4's still-open storage-shape decision needs.\n\n## Open questions for the user\n\n1. **Does the index move at all, and to where?** No destination path appears in any of the three documents. If the answer is \"yes, because Phase 6 makes entries mirror `corpus/` one-to-one\", say so explicitly — that is the only justification that holds. If it is \"for path hygiene\", the move is not worth its cost and should be dropped.\n2. **Are the 772 index manifest records deleted or rewritten?** R2.4 says rewrite, R2.6 says exclude from ingestion, Gate R1 says zero records under the new path. Those are three incompatible end-states. Note the rewrite covers only 522 distinct paths (126 appear up to 3×) and 248 of the 772 are `status=failed`.\n3. **Which edge layer is authoritative — per-source `*-edges.csv` or `_synthesis/global-edges.csv`?** They are the same data serialized twice (Wendt: 307/305 on both sides, 100% intersection), and four entries disagree between layers (FCM 428 vs 452, Aristotle 246 vs 156, GM 878 vs 876, Phantasia 708 vs 706). Nothing in the repo records which is stale. This decides both Gate W1's edge count and W5.4's storage sizing.\n4. **What goes into the Phase 0 commit, and what happens to `compiled-index.json`?** Committing it locks in a +583/-55 diff nobody can classify as real change vs. known `canonicalTerms` reordering churn; excluding it means Phase 1 must land the deterministic sort before the artifact is ever baselined. Related: confirm the commit's pathspec explicitly, given `node_modules` is tracked with 376 modified files.\n5. **Which pushes are authorised, and what counts as \"off-machine\" for the sandbox backup?** Three candidate pushes (`feat/wraith-retrieval` — 11 local-only commits, `writing-pipeline-v3`, the tag), and three candidate destinations (CHIMERA `192.168.50.243`, Mac `192.168.50.10`, WRAITH), versus the same-machine fallback `/mnt/m`.",
