        "notes": "READ-ONLY audit. No file created, modified, moved, or deleted; scripts/compile-corpus-index.py was never executed (only read).\n\nVERDICT: §4's NODE column is exact — all 28 label counts reproduce with zero discrepancy. §4's EDGE column is exactly reproducible under a specific glob but semantically wrong. §4's UNIT column has five per-entry errors. The one-unparseable-file claim is right; its diagnosis is wrong.\n\nHOW EACH COLUMN WAS DERIVED\n- nodes: §9 recipe verbatim on the working-tree compiled-index.json.\n- units: structured unit-record JSONs, cross-checked against each entry's manifest.json (`total_units` / `len(units)`) wherever one exists. The handoff's number is reproduced by counting JSON files in the structured directory WITHOUT excluding manifest.json, which is where four of the five errors come from.\n- edges: non-empty data rows (header excluded) over rglob('*-edges.csv'). This glob — and only this glob — reproduces 17,736 and every §4 per-entry figure, including the three that look anomalous: A Rhetoric of Motives 420 (its 8 per-chapter files are named `edges.csv`, invisible to `*-edges.csv`), and GM 1,754 / In-Game 1,472 (their `global-edges-pre-canonical.csv` is likewise invisible).\n\nCORRECTED CENSUS — deltas only; every row not listed is confirmed exact.\n\nHEALTHY (header should read 13, not 11; 14 with Aristotle)\n| Entry | Nodes | Units §4 -> actual | Edges: rows / distinct |\n| Boredom Secondary (Part III) | 68 ok | 55 ok | 3,815 / 1,897 |\n| VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III) | 60 ok | 34 ok | 2,260 / 1,122 |\n| A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945) | 56 ok | 28 ok | 1,754 / 877 (+878 missed) |\n| In-Game (Calleja 2011) | 44 ok | 26 ok | 1,472 / 1,069 (+736 missed) |\n| A Rhetoric of Motives (Burke 1950) | 39 ok | 8 ok | 420 / 417 (+420 missed) |\n| Heidegger - Being and Time | 37 ok | 18 -> 17 | 284 / 284 |\n| Heidegger - BCAP | 37 ok | 14 -> 13 | 93 / 93 |\n| Uncomfortable Situations | 36 ok | 6 ok | 744 / 528 |\n| Heidegger and Rhetoric | 36 ok | 16 ok | 204 / 204 |\n| Von Uexkull - A Foray | 35 ok | 15 -> 14 | 152 / 151 |\n| Heidegger - FCM | 32 ok | 15 ok | 880 / 450 |\n| Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric | 25 ok | 10 ok | 56 / 56 |\n| Wendt - Design for Dasein | 15 ok | 7 -> 8 | 614 / 305 |\n| Aristotle - Complete Works | 199 across 10 labels, 72/72 hooks — both ok | 45 -> 34 | 402 / 368 |\n\nONTOLOGY-ONLY (5): all nodes, units (0) and edges (0) confirmed exact.\n\nUNREGISTERED BUT REAL (4)\n| Phantasia | 8 units ok | 1,414 rows / ~708 real (dedupe unreliable, see finding) | 41 concepts ok |\n| RDR2 Secondary | 12 ok | 1,012 / 506 | 21 concepts ok |\n| Emotion Secondary | 5 ok | 420 / 210 | 40 concepts ok |\n| Motion and Time | 1 ok | 58 / 58 | 5 files ok |\n\nTOTALS\n| nodes | 701 objects / 771 label-attributions (§4 columns sum to 771) |\n| units | §4 sums to 323; §1 claims 357; corrected 310 |\n| edges | 17,736 rows under the §4 glob; 19,770 rows on disk; ~9,762 distinct |\n| files/bytes | 1,848 / 41,711,698 — exact, zero drift; 1,759 / 35,291,087 excluding nested .backups |\n\nTHE THREE JSON SHAPES FOR PHASE 1B (HANDOFF:208) — precise key names. Note there are five files in four shapes, not three.\n\n1. PHANTASIA — corpus/index/Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary (1985-2017)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json\nTop-level dict: cluster (str), synthesized_from_units (list[8]), concept_count (int 41), reading_count (int 22), tier1_count (int 9), concepts (list[41]), readings (list[22]), debate_axes (list[4]), merge_notes (list[7]).\nConcepts are a FLAT list; all 41 items share exactly 8 keys: id, canonical_name, definition, centrality_tier (int), synonyms_merged (list[str]), appears_in_units (list[str]), domain, first_pdf_page_in_pipeline.\nRichest shape — the only one carrying definitions, ids (PHX-C-001), and synonyms. Maps almost 1:1 onto ontologyNodes (name/definition/aliases/centralityTier/units).\n\n2. RDR2 SECONDARY — corpus/index/Red Dead Redemption 2 Secondary (2019-2023)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json\nTop-level dict: entry (str), organizing_principle (str), strands (list[9]), concept_nodes (list[21]), reading_nodes (list[12]), dissertation_anchors (dict[3]).\nConcepts are a FLAT list under `concept_nodes`; 20 items have keys {concept, tier, units}, 1 item has {concept, role, tier, units}. Key is `concept` (not `canonical_name`), `tier` (not `centrality_tier`), `units` (not `appears_in_units`). No definition, no id. The adapter must synthesize both.\n\n3. EMOTION — corpus/index/Aristotelian Emotion Secondary (1975-2015)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json\nTop-level dict: cluster (str), concept_nodes (DICT, not list), reading_nodes (DICT), organizing_axis (str), counts (dict).\n`concept_nodes` is a dict keyed tier1 / tier2 / tier3 -> lists of 28 / 9 / 3 = 40. Each item has exactly {label, units}. Key is `label` (a third name for the same field); tier is carried by the DICT KEY, not a field. counts = {concept_instances_raw: 99, canonical_concepts: 40, readings_raw: 44}. `reading_nodes` is a differently-keyed dict: doxastic_pole / phantastic_pole / affirmation_intermediate / cross_cutting_convergent (24 total).\nThinnest and structurally the odd one out — the only nested-by-tier shape.\n\n4. (NOT IN THE HANDOFF) BOREDOM SECONDARY — .../Boredom Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json\nkeys: cluster, prefix, generatedAt, generatedBy, ontologyFormat ('header'), compilerNote, nodeCount (68), byType, byCentrality, canonicalTermCount (156), nodes (list[68]). Its `generatedBy` states it was produced by the compiler's own parse_header_ontology(), so it is already compiler-native; its compilerNote flags that the header branch hardcodes the filename 'book-level-ontology.md' and needs a filename fallback.\n\n5. (NOT IN THE HANDOFF) VR PEDAGOGY — .../VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json\nkeys: cluster, nodes (list[60]) only. Minimal.\n\nShapes 4 and 5 belong to entries that already register 68 and 60 nodes via markdown, so wiring their JSON risks double-counting unless Phase 1B routes format per entry rather than per file.\n\nig-10 REPAIR (HANDOFF:230) — the fix is one character. Change `],` to `},` at line 155 of corpus/index/In-Game (Calleja 2011)/Calleja - From Immersion to Incorporation/ig-10-incorporation.json. The object opened at :134 (`\"non_game_studies_anchor_theories\": {`) contains two well-formed sub-objects, lakoff_johnson (:135-145) and damasio (:146-154), and is then closed with an array bracket. `expected_game_loci` at :107-119 is well-formed and is not part of the defect; the \"lines 107-155\" span in the handoff is wrong."
