        "notes": "INVENTORY (repo root /home/dalton/projects/claudeflow-testing, branch feat/wraith-retrieval; excluding node_modules, .git, .backups, backups/, and sqlite binaries).\n\nRepo-wide raw scale for context: 4,662 matches across 617 files, 64,421 files searched. Excluding corpus/index's own self-references, 288 files hit. Restricting further to the live tree (dropping tmp/, .claude/worktrees/, logs/, *.pyc) leaves 63 files plus scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl.\n\nPYTHON (live tree) — hardcoded literal:\n- scripts/normalize-edges.py:37,38,39,40,41 — five full entry paths (quoted under CONFIRMED).\n- scripts/reason/reason_over_knowledge.py:199 — `Path(\"corpus/index/compiled-index.json\")`, relative, silent-null on miss.\n- scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:31 `CORPUS_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\"`, :32 OUTPUT; docstring :5.\n- scripts/merge-reasoning-edges.py:21 `COMPILED_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\" / \"compiled-index.json\"`; docstring :7; used :116-120.\nPYTHON — string-free joins / roots:\n- scripts/audit/core/missing_link_detector.py:439; scripts/audit/core/coverage_analyzer.py:470; scripts/audit/core/orphan_identifier.py:335 (also :295, :304).\n- scripts/god_learn/god_learn.py:755 (--root default), plumbed :338-340, :720-721.\n- scripts/ingest/audit_ingest.py:97 and scripts/ingest/verify_ingest.py:166 — absolute hardcoded /home/dalton/projects/claudeflow-testing/corpus.\n- scripts/ingest/watch_corpus.py:175 — --root default \"corpus\".\n- scripts/ingest/run_ingest_phase2.py:978 SKIP_DIRS (nothing excludes index), :1137 doc_id mint, :1686 path_rel-keyed prior-chunk lookup.\nDuplicates outside the live tree (same content, will drift if only one is fixed): tmp/backup-pre-ku-plan-2026-03-18/python-scripts/normalize-edges.py:37-41, tmp/bootstrap-edges.py:25-85, tmp/backup-pre-ku-plan-20260318/bootstrap-edges.py:25-85, tmp/analysis-upgrade/production-sandbox/src-worktree/scripts/** (full mirror), .claude/worktrees/boredom-cluster-phase4-5/scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:31.\n\nTYPESCRIPT/JS (live tree) — 4 files, no .js:\n- src/god-agent/cli/quality/endnote-generator.ts:31 — path.resolve('corpus', pathRel).\n- src/god-agent/shared/jsonl-loaders.ts:200 — resolve(root,'corpus','index','compiled-index.json'); silent null :203.\n- src/god-agent/retrieval/smart-retrieval-layer.ts:798 — resolve(process.cwd(),'corpus','index','compiled-index.json'); silent empty-set :799.\n- src/god-agent/shared/cross-author-utils.ts:10 (doc comment), :79 (manifest.jsonl path), :395-398 (dash split).\n- src/god-agent/universal/write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:1772, 3430, 4030 — comments only, no path construction.\n\nRUST — none (see new_findings).\n\nSHELL — zero hits in the live tree. scripts/setup/setup-target.sh:161,168 invoke god_learn.py without --root and therefore inherit the :755 default. All 16 .sh hits are inside tmp/analysis-upgrade/{sandbox,production-sandbox,integration-sandbox}, which use their own $SANDBOX_ROOT/data/corpus/index and an already-parameterized CORPUS_INDEX_PATH env var (e.g. production-sandbox/scripts/run-step4-post3b.sh:31) — the sandbox is the one subsystem that got this right and is a usable pattern for R2.\n\nMARKDOWN / PLANS — 63 live-tree files, documentation only (plans/ is not under the ingest root, so none of it is walked by run_ingest_phase2.py). Heaviest: plans/rickert-ambient-rhetoric-analysis.md (31), plans/heidegger-bt-analysis.md (21), plans/heidegger-bcap-analysis.md (18), plans/boredom-experiment-index-entry-plan-2026-07-10.md (16), plans/citation-enrichment-phase-2-execution-plan.md (14), plans/secondary-cluster-index-plan-TEMPLATE-2026-07-15.md (12), plans/index-system-report-2026-07-28.md (11), plans/index-system-HANDOFF-2026-07-28.md (10), docs/research/ku-reasoning-edge-system-analysis.md (11). The TEMPLATE file matters more than its size suggests — it seeds every future cluster plan with the old path.\n\nJSON / CONFIG — effectively zero. The only live-tree hits are scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl (772 data records, not config) and plans/archon-video-policy.toml:13 (prose in a comment). No .claude/settings.json, hook, package.json, or .agentdb/.god-agent/.claude/runtime store references the path at all.\n\nSQLITE BINARIES (reported separately, per instruction) — vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3 is the only one carrying the string: 458 strings-lines / 497 raw occurrences / 319 live-table occurrences (175 embedding_metadata + 144 FTS content), across 67 embedding_metadata rows (41 chroma:document, 25 path_abs, 1 raw_content). .chroma-data/chroma.sqlite3 = 0, .agentdb-test/chroma.sqlite3 = 0, backups/pre-migration-2026-03-26/vector_db_1536.bak/chroma.sqlite3 = 0, backups/pre-ocr-20260128-095213/vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3 = 0. All queries run read-only via `file:...?mode=ro&immutable=1`; no file was written.\n\nBLAST-RADIUS RANKING (worst first, if missed during Phase 2):\n\n1. run_ingest_phase2.py path_rel/doc_id namespace (:221-223, :659, :699, :1137, :1686). Silent, unbounded, and irreversible-by-default: 522 distinct index documents mint fresh doc_ids, the path_rel-keyed cleanup no-ops, and the old chunks persist as an invisible shadow corpus that retrieval will happily return alongside the new one. Nothing in the pipeline detects the duplication.\n\n2. scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl (772 records / 522 paths). Every other consumer keys off path_rel — doc_id minting, endnote bbox rendering, all three audit scripts, corpus-validator, and deriveAuthor's canonical author/title tables (cross-author-utils.ts:96-167 reads only status=='ok' rows). Stale path_rel silently shrinks those tables, which pushes deriveAuthor from branches 2/3 down into the dash-split branch 4 — precisely the failure mode §5.4 warns about, arriving by the manifest rather than by a rename.\n\n3. compile-corpus-index.py roots — :31 CORPUS_INDEX, :35-… TEXT_DIRS (19 dir-name keys), :1239 hardcoded Aristotle dir. Failure is total and silent: :1264-1265 `continue` on a missing dir, and losing the Aristotle dir zeroes all 72 crossPipelineHooks, which kills getActiveBridges() and with it the entire author-scoped supplemental retrieval branch (icp-orchestrator.ts:366-390, write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:1868/:2003). §5.1 already says a clean run proves nothing; this is the sharpest instance.\n\n4. god_learn.py:755 plus audit_ingest.py:97 / verify_ingest.py:166. One keystroke (/god-learn-compile) re-walks whatever root is baked in. If the index moves out of corpus/ this silently stops ingesting it (no error, manifest just stops growing); if it moves within corpus/ it re-ingests everything under new doc_ids, compounding #1. The two absolute defaults are worse — they ignore repo relocation entirely.\n\n5. The four string-free path-join sites. endnote-generator.ts:31 breaks bbox/highlight rendering for every index-sourced citation (visible-ish: renders just stop appearing). The three audit scripts fail silently and, worse, invert their verdicts — coverage_analyzer returns 0 pages (0% coverage), orphan_identifier reports every index PDF as an orphan, missing_link_detector reports intact chains as broken. A Phase 2 run that trusts these tools as verification will read a catastrophic report as a real regression, or vice versa.\n\n6. compiled-index.json loaders (jsonl-loaders.ts:200, smart-retrieval-layer.ts:798, reason_over_knowledge.py:199, merge-reasoning-edges.py:21). All silent; smart-retrieval-layer's empty protected-term set is the nastiest because it silently reopens the C-03 stopword regression its own comment claims to fix, degrading retrieval quality with no log line. Note §5.9 — this would be indistinguishable from a bad retrieval experiment.\n\n7. The 219 ingested self-referencing index files. Not a break, but it makes the stated exit gate unreachable and will keep generating false positives in every future path audit.\n\n8. .claude/worktrees/boredom-cluster-phase4-5 (own corpus/index + compiler:31) and the tmp/ mirrors. Contained blast radius, but they are live git worktrees, so a later merge can reintroduce old-path code into the main tree.\n\n9. normalize-edges.py:37-41. Loud failure (FileNotFoundError), dev-only tooling, five lines to fix. Lowest of the code sites despite being the most conspicuous string match.\n\n10. plans/ and docs/ markdown (63 files). Cosmetic — not ingested, not executed. Only plans/secondary-cluster-index-plan-TEMPLATE-2026-07-15.md deserves priority, because it propagates the old path into every future cluster plan.\n\nMETHOD NOTE — everything above is read-only: rg/grep/find/wc, `python3 -c` reads, and sqlite3 opened with mode=ro&immutable=1 (no WAL/SHM created). scripts/compile-corpus-index.py was never executed. Two scratch files were written outside the repo, under the session scratchpad: sim_derive.py (the deriveAuthor simulation) and selfrefs.txt."
      }
