          },
          {
            "risk": "Phase 0's tracking commit and Phase 2's manifest rewrite both trip GitHub Actions workflows that no document in the programme mentions. `.github/workflows/god-audit.yml:5-21` triggers on paths `corpus/**`, `god-reason/**`, `scripts/ingest/**`, `vector_db_1536/**` and runs `python3 scripts/audit/core/missing_link_detector.py --all --json` (:56) - which is one of the four string-free path-join sites R2.3 must change (`missing_link_detector.py:439`). `.github/workflows/god-learn-qa.yml:41-53` runs `verify_knowledge.py --strict_order`, `verify_reasoning.py --strict_order`, and `scripts/explore/verify/immutability_checker.py --verify`, whose protected-path list (`immutability_checker.py:110-122`) includes `scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` and `god-reason/reasoning.jsonl` - exactly the two files R2.4 and Phase 3 mutate.",
            "phases_involved": "0 (D2 staging), 2 (R2.3, R2.4), 3 (N3.2)",
            "why": "Zero occurrences of 'github', 'workflow', 'CI', or 'actions' in the handoff, report, or implementation plan (grep across all three; the only 'workflow' hits are the human-workflow rule at HANDOFF:175 and plan:300). The immutability baseline `.god-verify/immutability_baseline.json` is dated Jan 13 2026 and the checker has no caller outside its own README, so nobody has observed it fail - but the workflow will invoke it.",
            "mitigation": "Before Phase 0: decide explicitly whether these workflows are live, and either re-baseline `immutability_baseline.json` as a Phase 2 deliverable or add both workflow files to the R2.2/R2.3 change list. Add `.github/workflows/` to the Phase 2 sweep inventory."
          },
          {
            "risk": "Gate R1's verification step mutates the artifact Phase 2 just rewrote. `/god-learn-verify` runs `scripts/god_learn/god_learn.py verify` (`.claude/commands/god-learn-verify.md:7`), and `cmd_verify` (`god_learn.py:711-718`) calls `deduplicate_manifest(rr, log_path)` as its FIRST action. `deduplicate_manifest` ('Keep only the latest manifest entry per path_abs') rewrites `scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` in place, collapsing 1,182 records to ~696 and destroying the 248 `status=failed` index records - keyed on `path_abs`, so post-move old and new paths survive as two independent keys.",
            "phases_involved": "2 (R2.4 then Gate R1)",
            "why": "The gate is written as a read-only check ('/god-learn-verify passes'). It is a write. No phase backs up manifest.jsonl before it runs, and the file carries the only record of which index documents failed ingestion.",
            "mitigation": "Snapshot `scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl` into the timestamped backup before R2.4 and again before Gate R1; state in the gate that it dedups by `path_abs` and therefore cannot be used to prove the old paths are gone."
          },
          {
            "risk": "Phase 3's relation-vocabulary collapse silently invalidates a second, undocumented runtime substrate. `scripts/normalize-edges.py:37-41` feeds 5 hardcoded index `global-edges.csv` files into `scripts/merge-reasoning-edges.py`, which writes `god-reason/reasoning.jsonl` (21,498,945 bytes, git-tracked). That file has ~20 consumers - including `src/god-agent/observability/explore-bridge.ts`, `src/god-agent/observability/icp-api-routes.ts`, `scripts/explore/core/artifact_loader.py:137`, `scripts/graph-visualize.py`, `scripts/knowledge-prune.py`, `scripts/compute-corroboration.py`, `scripts/backfill-edge-ku-links.py`, `scripts/migrate-bridge-edges.py`, `scripts/sync-ku-to-memory.py` - none of which the report identifies (report §3 names only four).",
            "phases_involved": "2 (R2.9), 3 (N3.2, N3.5), 5",
            "why": "R2.9/N3.5 say to update `normalize-edges.py`'s paths and extend it, but no item says to REBUILD `reasoning.jsonl`, re-run `merge-reasoning-edges.py`, or re-derive the KU links. Collapsing 633 relation values changes the vocabulary the observability graph and KU corroboration scores are keyed on.",
            "mitigation": "Add an N3.6: 'rebuild god-reason/reasoning.jsonl from the normalized edge layer; enumerate and re-validate its consumers'. Snapshot `god-reason/` alongside `corpus/index` in the pre-Phase-3 backup."
          },
          {
            "risk": "Phase 1B's target state ('JSON is the machine-readable ontology for every entry') collides with two entries that already register via markdown AND ship JSON. `corpus/index/Boredom Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json` (nodeCount 68; its `generatedBy` records it was produced by the compiler's own parse_header_ontology) and `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/_synthesis/cluster-ontology.json` (60 nodes) coexist with the `cluster-ontology.md` the compiler reads today. 1B is scoped as '+102 concepts from three unregistered clusters' and does not say the json branch must be per-entry-exclusive.",
            "phases_involved": "1 (1B, Gate C1)",
            "why": "There are FIVE `cluster-ontology.json` files under corpus/index, not three. A naive `ontology_format: \"json\"` dispatch that also fires for these two entries double-counts 128 nodes, and Gate C1's only node-count assertion is 'the 3 JSON clusters register with non-zero nodes' - which a doubled total still satisfies.",
            "mitigation": "State in 1B that ontology_format is a per-entry exclusive selector, and add to Gate C1: 'total ontologyNodes = 701 + 102 +/- the declared delta, itemized per entry'."
          },
          {
            "risk": "Phase 6 adds ~140 entries while `.claude/CORPUS-ONLY-CONSTRAINT.md` - a frozen citable-source allowlist last updated 2026-01-30, listing ~39 works against 288 corpus PDFs - remains the operative constraint for the drafting agents. It is cited by `.claude/commands/god-write.md:11`, `.claude/commands/god-complete-section.md:11`, and 11 agents under `.claude/agents/phdresearch/` (e.g. literature-review-writer.md, evidence-synthesizer.md, gap-hunter.md).",
            "phases_involved": "6 (E6.1-E6.4); also 4, for the repaired ontology-only entries",
            "why": "No phase owns this file. Every new entry authored in Phase 6 describes a source the drafting agents are told they may not cite, and the failure mode is silent omission rather than error.",
            "mitigation": "Make the allowlist a generated artifact of the entry registry (Phase 1C / W5.5) rather than a hand-maintained markdown file, and add regeneration to Gate E1."
          },
          {
            "risk": "R2.5 purges 25 ingested index chunks from ChromaDB before the move, but no item backs up `vector_db_1536/` (6.5 GB) first, and the purge has no implementation. The only delete call in the ingest tree is `run_ingest_phase2.py:1830` `coll.delete(ids=_stale)`, driven by a `coll.get(where={\"path_rel\": path_rel})` lookup at :1686 - which returns nothing once the path has changed, making the built-in stale-cleanup a no-op across a relocation.",
            "phases_involved": "2 (R2.5)",
            "why": "The plan says 'purge before move' as if a purge tool exists. `ls scripts/ingest/` contains no purge or reset script. Whatever is written will be a first-run destructive operation against a 6.5 GB store that no backup covers.",
            "mitigation": "Add a P0-class item: `sqlite3 .backup` of `vector_db_1536/chroma.sqlite3` before any delete; write the purge as a `doc_id`-keyed (not `path_rel`-keyed) script with a dry-run mode and a recorded before/after count."
          }
        ],
        "gate_weaknesses": [
          {
            "gate": "Gate P0 - 'tracking applied - branch and tag resolve on origin - sandbox data byte-verified in a second location'",
            "weakness": "Covers `corpus/index` (45 MB) and `production-sandbox/data` (50 MB) but not `corpus/` itself: 2.7 GB across rhetorical_ontology 1.5G, new_media 461M, metaphysics 178M, boredom 153M, biomedical_engineering 131M, download 124M, textual_analysis 99M, pedagogy 57M, Virtual Learning Environments 43M, AD(H)D 23M. `git ls-files corpus | grep -v '^corpus/index/'` returns 0 tracked files; `git status --porcelain -uall corpus` shows 3,079 untracked non-index paths; none are gitignored. These 288 PDFs are the entire input to Phase 6 (~140 new entries) and to any re-ingest in Phase 2, and no backup on this machine covers them.",
            "stronger_gate": "Gate P0 additionally requires: a hash manifest of `corpus/` (non-index) verified in a second location, OR an explicit written decision that the 288 source PDFs are re-acquirable and therefore out of scope - recorded, not assumed."
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate C1 - 'two consecutive runs byte-identical'",
            "weakness": "Unachievable as stated regardless of the sort fix: `compile-corpus-index.py:1375` writes `\"builtAt\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()` unconditionally, so every run differs. The gate also asserts nothing about the two largest classes of data the compiler still cannot see after 1A/1B: 144 `cross_pipeline_bridges` entries across 22 unit JSONs under corpus/index (vs 72 hooks in the artifact, 100% Aristotle), and 1,544 arrow-edges encoded in 67 `.mmd` files across 15 entries.",
            "stronger_gate": "'Two consecutive runs byte-identical with builtAt injected/frozen; --check fails on a corrupted fixture; the run prints a per-entry table of nodes/hooks/tensions/edges-seen vs edges-skipped, and the sum of skipped is zero or explicitly waived per entry.'"
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate R1 - 'fresh Chroma build has zero hits outside the 39'",
            "weakness": "Cannot pass. 296 files inside `corpus/index` contain the literal string `corpus/index` in their own prose (1,800 line-hits; e.g. `corpus/index/A Grammar of Motives (Burke 1945)/_synthesis/phase0-overview.md:7,51,225,240,275,289`), and 219 of those are already manifest-ingested with status ok. Any re-ingestion under the new path reproduces every one of those strings inside chunk text. R2.10 sweeps the prose but the gate is measured on a `strings` count that mixes line-counts (458) with row-counts (39) in different units.",
            "stronger_gate": "'Zero rows in embedding_metadata with key in {path_rel, path_abs, doc_id} whose value contains the old path' - a table-and-field-scoped assertion, with prose self-references handled by R2.10 and counted separately."
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate N1 - 'all 27 entries load through the adapter layer into the canonical type; validator passes'",
            "weakness": "The canonical unit record defined at N3.1 ('id, entry, title, locus range, concepts, arguments, claims, edges, provenance') has no slot for the richest payload on disk. 35 `*-deep.json` files (Burke GM 14, Burke RM 8, Calleja In-Game 13) carry positions (35/35), tensions (35/35), interlocutors (34), outline (33), cross_pipeline_bridges (17), philosophers_cited (14), game_loci (13), candidate_augmentation_mappings (11), literary_examples (9), pentad_term_tags (8), calleja_pim_candidates (8), dimension_operational_definition (7), paradigm_worked_examples (6), residual_phenomenology_anchor_sites (4), philosophic_school_mapping (3). `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` §2 already flags these as 'the single richest file in the corpus'. A validator that passes on N3.1's field list certifies the loss.",
            "stronger_gate": "'The canonical record is a superset: for every entry the adapter emits a `residual` map containing every source key not mapped to a named field, and the validator FAILS if any residual map is discarded rather than carried. Field-coverage report per adapter family, reconciled against plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:45-58.'"
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate Q1 - 'zero unparseable files'",
            "weakness": "Scoped to JSON only (the §9 recipe globs `*.json`). No parse or schema gate exists for the other 965 non-JSON artifacts: 240 `.csv` (42 header dialects), 67 `.mmd`, 27 `.txt`, 2 `.jsonl` (perplexity-escalation-log.jsonl), 3 `.html`, 2 `.tex`. Separately, Q4.6 ('install mmdc; render validation has never been performed') is factually a no-op - mmdc IS installed at `/home/dalton/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/bin/mmdc`, version 11.14.0, and render validation HAS run: `corpus/index/Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary (1985-2017)/_synthesis/render-validation.txt` (2026-05-11, 5 graphs PASS, 'mmdc v11.14.0') and `corpus/index/Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/render-validation.txt` (2026-05-10). The real gap is that 13 of the 15 `.mmd`-bearing entries have no render-validation record, and only 5 entries commit `.svg` renders (25 files, all in Aristotle/BT/BCAP/Rickert/Uexkull).",
            "stronger_gate": "'Every .mmd renders under mmdc 11.14.0 and every entry with .mmd files carries a render-validation.txt with node/edge counts against its declared caps; every .csv parses under its declared dialect; every .jsonl parses line-by-line.' Delete the 'install mmdc' item and replace it with the 13-entry backfill."
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate W1 - 'a Uexkull-scoped query returns his units, concepts, arguments, and 152 edges without a vector search'",
            "weakness": "Named on one of the thinner entries and enumerates only the four things W5.1/W5.2 already emit. It does not require the entry's 5 `.mmd` graphs (111 arrow-edges), its concept-matrix.csv, its `uex-analysis/tension-edges.json`, or its unit prose. Scoping the gate to Uexkull means a wiring layer that drops every apparatus type below can still pass.",
            "stronger_gate": "Run the gate on the richest entry instead - 'a query scoped to A Grammar of Motives returns its 28 units INCLUDING the 14 -deep.json payloads (positions, tensions, interlocutors, ratio catalog, philosophic-school mapping), its concept-matrix, its 5 mermaid graphs, its bibliography-extracted and interlocutor-map, and its edges' - and keep Uexkull as the cheap smoke test."
          },
          {
            "gate": "D4 / Phase 1C - 'analysis-artifact entries are excluded from source-entry gates but still reachable by entry-scoped retrieval'",
            "weakness": "A promise with no gate and no implementing item anywhere. The four entries hold file types no W5.x item emits: `Red Dead Redemption 2 (Salvo Playthrough)` = 96 .md + 22 .vtt + 22 .txt transcripts + 1 json (141 files, zero units and zero edges by the census); `Game-Behavior Analysis Method (Burke x Calleja)` = 33 files including 3 .pdf, 3 .html, 2 .tex, build_pdf.py, 9 versions of CANONICAL-METHODOLOGY, 7 VALIDATION-*.md and THE-MATRIX.md; `Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)` = 9 files of RODA matrices and frame traces; `Dissertation` = run-history. 'Excluded from the ontology compile' + 'no synthesis layer' + 'nothing in W5.1-5.3 emits transcripts or LaTeX' equals unreachable.",
            "stronger_gate": "'For each analysis-artifact entry, a scoped query returns a named, enumerated set of its files - with the retrieval representation stated per file type (transcript, methodology doc, RODA matrix, run-history) - verified by one query per entry.'"
          },
          {
            "gate": "Gate E1 / Phase 6 scale figures, and D2's 'track everything else'",
            "weakness": "Phase 6 sizing rests on the same `*-edges.csv` glob and unit-count method the audits already showed wrong in both directions, and no gate re-derives them. Separately, 8 empty directories exist under corpus/index (`VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/units`, `Boredom Secondary (Part III)/units`, `Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric/rickert-analysis-experiments`, `Game-Behavior Analysis Method/figures`, plus 4 under Dissertation), which git cannot represent - so D2's 'track everything else' does not preserve the tree shape the D1 rsync backup captured, and the file-count verification will not notice.",
            "stronger_gate": "Gate P0 adds 'the set of directories present in the backup tree but absent from `git ls-files` is enumerated and either populated with a .gitkeep or explicitly waived'; Gate E1 adds 'per-entry counts re-derived by the Phase 3 validator, not by filename glob'."
          }
        ],
        "underspecified": [
          "The apparatus inventory in W5.3 names five artifact types ('concept matrices, debate maps, citation networks, contested nodes, terminology appendices'). The _synthesis/ layer holds ~200 distinct filenames. Types present on disk and named NOWHERE in the handoff, report, or implementation plan: `*-loci-concordance.{md,json}` (8 files - aes-aristotle, hr-aristotle, hr-heidegger, phx-aristotle, us-emotion, us-literary, us-neuroscience, us-rhetoric - this is the 'concordance grid' the quality gates are defined over), `*-bibliography-extracted.{md,json}` (gm, hr, ig, us), `*-interlocutor-map.{md,json}` (gm, hr, ig, us), `*-secondary-literature-network.{md,json}` (aes, boredom, phx, rdr, vr-pedagogy - distinct from citation-network), `*-scholarly-evolution*.md` (5), `contested-readings.md` (5, distinct from the contested-nodes.md W5.3 does name), `drafting-loci.md` (3), `citations.md` (3), and the operationalization manuals: gm-pentad-operationalization-manual, gm-four-master-tropes-manual, gm-applied-dramatism-walkthroughs, gm-ratio-catalog, gm-substance-vocabulary, gm-philosophic-school-mapping, ig-pim-operationalization-manual, rm-identification-consubstantiation-manual, rm-pentad-extension-patch, rm-attitude-as-sixth-term, dfd-vle-design-manual, fcm-boredom-attunement-manual, fcm-king-salvo-bridge, dfd-rhetorical-ontology-bridge, bridge-to-part-ii.md, pathe-to-diss-section-map.md. These manuals are the applied-method artifacts - the ones a drafting prompt would most want. Belongs in Phase 1 (census) and Phase 5 (W5.3).",
          "67 `.mmd` mermaid files across 15 entries encode 1,544 arrow-edges (Aristotle 245, In-Game 187, Heidegger and Rhetoric 133, BCAP 116, GM 111, Uexkull 111, Phantasia 109, Uncomfortable 109, VR Pedagogy 104, Boredom Secondary 102, BT 88, Rickert 80, RDR2 Sec 20, RM 18, Boredom Experiment 11). The programme's entire edge story is the 17,736 CSV rows; `.mmd` appears only as a rendering chore (Q4.6). `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` §2 records for BOTH the aristotle-manifest and heidegger-sz adapter families that 'Edges live only in .mmd (open item)' - so for Aristotle and Being and Time the mermaid graphs may be the only edge representation. W5.2 and N3.2 have no mermaid adapter. Belongs in Phase 3 (N3.2/N3.3) and Phase 5 (W5.2).",
          "144 `cross_pipeline_bridges` entries live in 22 unit JSON files under corpus/index, plus 11 non-Aristotle cross-pipeline artifacts (gm-graph-cross-pipeline-bridge.mmd, rm-, hr-, ig-, us-, phx-, rdr-graph- plus rdr-cross-pipeline-bridge.md, uex-graph-cross-pipeline.mmd/.svg, and graph-cross-pipeline-bridge.mmd in both Boredom Secondary and VR Pedagogy). Runtime has 72 hooks, 100% Aristotle, because the compiler globs `*-cross-pipeline-hooks.md` only under `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works` (compile-corpus-index.py:1239-1244). D6 declares 'all 72 hooks' as evidence Aristotle is healthy; it is also the evidence that roughly two thirds of the authored bridge inventory is invisible. No phase item covers it - 1B is about ontology nodes, not hooks. Belongs in Phase 1 (alongside 1B) and Phase 5.",
          "The `bridge-sources/` directory type appears in 6 entries and is mentioned once in the whole programme (report §1.1, as a layout label). It is not in W5.3 and has no adapter. `Wendt - Design for Dasein/bridge-sources/` (11 files) holds `roda-crosswalk.md` - the artifact `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` maps to a dedicated `corpus_roda_crosswalks` relation - plus a full `bme-vr-env-analysis/` sub-study with 3 session transcripts (transcript-group.txt, transcript-windows.txt, transcript-mediaplayer.txt) and 4 keyframe .jpg files. `Heidegger - FCM/bridge-sources/` holds 3 king-salvo digests (eyetracking, phenomenological, physiological). VLE, Boredom Experiment, Boredom Secondary and VR Pedagogy hold paper-digest-pointers.md / anchor-pointers.md. Belongs in Phase 3 (adapter) and Phase 5 (W5.3).",
          "The Dissertation entry's per-run pipeline apparatus is uncounted and unclassified beyond 'analysis-artifact'. On disk: phase0-overview.md x19, phase1-metadata.json x14, phase2-{narrative,claims,edges,claims.json,narrative-delta} x12 each, citation-gap-table.{md,json} x12 each, revision-checklist.md x12, phase2-lanham-profile.json x6, INHERITED-FROM-PRIOR.md x6, plus citation-gap-master, citation-gap-resolution, master-citation-report-parsed.json, numbering-audit, relocations, revision-roadmap, diagram-renumbering-patch, page-offset-verification, canonical-id-resolution-report, terminology-reckoning, terminology-decisions-final, inconsistencies-and-fallacies, inter-contributor-disagreements, proposals-for-user-judgment, hawhee-correction-evidence, burke-correction-evidence, cache-coverage-summary. These encode the drafting pipeline's own citation-gap and correction history - arguably the highest-value retrieval target for a revision session - and no phase mentions any of them. Belongs in Phase 1C (classification) and Phase 5 (D4 reachability).",
          "A whole apparatus family for external-source enrichment is unnamed: perplexity-queue.{md,json} x2, perplexity-summary.md x2, perplexity-budget-allocation.md x2, perplexity-escalation-log.jsonl x2, perplexity-downloads-flagged-for-deep-analysis.md x2, perplexity-downloads-deep-analysis-final.md x2, deep-analysis-source-digests.md x2, corpus-routing-plan.{md,json} x2, phase4-0-ingest-summary.md x2. `corpus-routing-plan` in particular is a machine-readable statement of where an entry's sources were routed inside corpus/ - directly relevant to report §7's 'nine entries have no machine-readable source path' (Q4.8) and to Phase 6 provenance - and is never cited. Belongs in Phase 4 (Q4.8) and Phase 6 (E6.6).",
          "`scripts/explore/verify/immutability_checker.py` is verification that is claimed and never runs. Its docstring (:90-101) declares god-learn/knowledge.jsonl, god-reason/reasoning.jsonl, scripts/ingest/manifest.jsonl and corpus/rhetorical_ontology immutable; its baseline `.god-verify/immutability_baseline.json` is dated Jan 13 2026 and has not been regenerated; grep for immutability_checker|ImmutabilityChecker across the repo (excluding node_modules and the sandbox worktree) returns only its own file and two READMEs - plus `.github/workflows/god-learn-qa.yml:53`, the only actual invocation, which fires only on push/PR to main. Phase 2 rewrites two of its four protected artifacts. Belongs in Phase 0 (decide disposition) and Phase 2 (re-baseline).",
          "An unresolved index CONTENT defect queue exists and no phase absorbs it. `docs/actualization-chain/index-ku-issues-report.md` (2026-04-17, 'for human review only') lists five specific Aristotle-entry defects: pathe tes psuches under-weighted in aristotle-graph-psychology.mmd with missing edges to orexis/alloiosis; De Insomniis 460b3-16 has no unit analysis in Aristotle - Complete Works; global-edges.csv lacks the RHET-03 to DA-04 cross-work edges; MA-01's pathe ambiguity at 702a17 is unflagged; doxa is absent from the De Anima ontology's node list. Phase 4 is entirely structural (malformed JSON, broken paths, zero-yield tension files, missing manifests). D6 declares the Aristotle entry 'healthy' on node/hook counts, which is orthogonal to these. Belongs in Phase 4 (a new 4E, content defects).",
          "Phase 6 assumes the source substrate is safe and present, but corpus/ outside the index is 2.7 GB across 3,079 untracked, unignored, un-backed-up files (`git ls-files corpus | grep -v index` = 0). The plan's own `git clean -fd` warning (plan:112) is scoped to the index; the same command would take the 288 PDFs Phase 6 depends on and the 1.5 GB rhetorical_ontology that immutability_checker.py:121 declares protected. Belongs in Phase 0.",
          "`vector_db_1536/` (6.5 GB) has no backup step anywhere, yet R2.5 deletes from it and Gate R1 requires 'a fresh Chroma build'. No item states whether 'fresh build' means re-embedding the whole ~413k-chunk corpus (cost and duration unstated, and the local embedder on :8000 was down at audit time) or a targeted rebuild. Belongs in Phase 0 (backup) and Phase 2 (define 'fresh build').",
          "The `*-structured/` + `*-analysis/` layout pair (Being and Time, BCAP, Uexkull, Rickert) is named in report §1.1 as a layout but never given an adapter or a wiring item; `Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric/rickert-analysis-experiments/` is an empty third variant directory whose purpose is undocumented. These four entries are also the only ones that commit rendered `.svg` (25 files) alongside `.mmd`, so they carry a two-representation convention nothing accounts for. Belongs in Phase 3 (N3.3).",
          "`aristotle-bekker-index.json` (188 entries per plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md §2) and the 9 `*-greek.json` files plus `aristotle-greek-appendix.json` are an entry-specific lemma/locus apparatus with no place in N3.1's canonical record and no mention in any phase. They are the mechanism by which a Bekker citation resolves to a unit - directly load-bearing for the dissertation's citation rigor. Note also that the handoff's 45-unit figure for Aristotle counts these 11 apparatus files as units. Belongs in Phase 3 (N3.1) and Phase 5 (W5.3).",
          "The programme never reconciles itself with `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` (2026-06-24) beyond a single pointer at N3.3. That spec already performed the adapter census Phase 3 defers, already identified the -DEEP.json files as the crown jewels, already flagged the .mmd-only edge problem for Aristotle and Heidegger, and already lists per-family 'crown-jewel fields that MUST land' (design_principles, ro_hooks, mediation_relations, object_types_present, anchor_phrases, key_terms.gloss, aristotle_exegesis_table, aquinas_exegesis, act_term_operationalization, ratio_catalog, readings, themes, debate_axis_positions, cluster_citations, sections). Phase 3 restating the problem from scratch risks producing a narrower canonical type than the one already specified. Belongs in Phase 3 (N3.1-N3.3).",
          "Two `coverage_analyzer.py` files exist - `scripts/audit/core/coverage_analyzer.py:470` (named in R2.3) and `scripts/explore/core/coverage_analyzer.py` (unnamed). The whole `scripts/explore/` subsystem (cli/god_explore.py, core/graph_builder.py, core/artifact_loader.py:137, visualization/d3_viewer.html, graph.json) is an index-derived exploration/visualization layer the report never identifies as a consumer. Belongs in Phase 2 (path sweep) and Phase 3 (edge-vocabulary consumers).",
          "D2's 'track everything else' is unspecified about binary and generated artifacts inside the index: 4 .pdf, 4 .jpg, 3 .html, 25 .svg, 2 .log, 1 .aux, 1 .py (build_pdf.py), plus Game-Behavior-Analysis-Method.{tex,pdf,log} and RODA-Walkthrough-BarFight.{tex,pdf,log,aux} - LaTeX build products checked in alongside sources. No policy states whether generated PDFs/SVGs/logs are tracked, regenerated, or ignored, and Gate P0's file-count verification will silently encode whichever choice is made. Belongs in Phase 0 (D2)."
        ],
        "recommended_first_moves": [
          {
            "move": "Freeze a machine-readable apparatus census before Phase 1 touches anything: for all 27 entries, emit one row per file with (entry, relative path, extension, apparatus type, byte size, whether any code reads it today). Store it under plans/ next to the handoff. Seed it from the figures already verified here: 1,848 files / 41,711,698 bytes; 865 .md (691 unit prose, 10,989,962 bytes), 494 .json, 240 .csv, 67 .mmd (1,544 arrow-edges), 27 .txt, 25 .svg, 22 .vtt, 4 .pdf, 4 .jpg, 3 .html, 2 .tex, 2 .jsonl, 2 .log, 1 .py, 1 .aux, plus 8 empty directories.",
